      "text": "placed … Cherubims, and a flaming sword, Gen. 3:24 (Alma 12:21–29; 42:2–3; Moses 4:31). make two cherubims of gold, Ex. 25:18 (37:6–9). make the tabernacle … with cherubims of cunning work, Ex. 26:1. heard the voice … between the two cherubims, Num. 7:89. Lord … dwelleth between the cherubims, 1 Sam. 4:4 (2 Sam. 6:2; Ps. 80:1; 99:1; Isa. 37:16). he rode upon a cherub, and did fly, 2 Sam. 22:11. he made two cherubims of olive tree, 1 Kgs. 6:23. cherubims spread forth their two wings, 1 Kgs. 8:7 (2 Chr. 5:8; Ezek. 10:19). in the most holy house he made two cherubims of image work, 2 Chr. 3:10. glory of the God of Israel was gone up from the cherub, Ezek. 9:3. Thou art the anointed cherub that covereth, Ezek. 28:14.",
